From 9f1a2c4d8e7b4a3c9d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 14:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(broker): bind task runs to durable three-plane project workspaces

Broker tasks now render the three-plane contract in the worker context
(`/workspace/work`, read-only `/workspace/inputs`, writable `/workspace/output`)
alongside the frozen Project, revision, source-generation binding, and
effective permission. The trusted catalogue pins the broker-project provider
revision, refuses untrusted Project providers, and leaves the source
generation unset until trusted dispatch binds it through the broker resolve
RPC instead of inventing one from the template.

The pre-spawn workspace service activates the exact task run with the broker
(resolve, acquire, activate) and reports the guest planes; the Gondolin
client gains typed resolve_project_source and authority_status calls so
trusted external workers map a durable workspace binding to its host work
plane without ever seeing the guest path. Guest workers receive the plane
layout and Project authority facts through the isolated environment contract.
---

